# =========================================================================================== #
# File: '.gitignore'
# --- [ Description ] ----------------------------------------------------------------------- #
#
# DEFAULT-DENY, EXPLICIT INCLUDES ONLY. Nothing in this working tree is tracked unless it is
# explicitly allowed below, by name — no wildcard allowances. Adding a new file therefore
# requires allowing it here first — that is deliberate: it makes publishing a file an
# explicit act rather than an accident.
#
# Note the deliberate absence: materialized role scripts (the .ps1 a role stub resolves to,
# e.g. ansible/applications/fileserver/files/Set-SmbServerHardening.ps1) are build artifacts
# of scripts/materialize-role-scripts.sh and are never allowlisted. Only the .ps1.stub marker
# is tracked; the script itself is tracked once, under powershell/.
#
# =========================================================================================== #

# Ignore everything ...
**

# --- [ directory spine ] -------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# Git does not descend into an excluded directory, so every directory on the path to an
# allowed file is re-included by name. This publishes no files by itself: files inside these
# directories stay ignored until named in a section below.
!/.github/
!/.github/workflows/
!/ansible/
!/ansible/applications/
!/ansible/applications/fileserver/
!/ansible/applications/fileserver/defaults/
!/ansible/applications/fileserver/files/
!/ansible/applications/fileserver/meta/
!/ansible/applications/fileserver/tasks/
!/ansible/applications/fileserver/vars/
!/ansible/inventory/
!/ansible/playbooks/
!/docs/
!/docs/explanation/
!/docs/reference/
!/scripts/

# --- [ allowed: repository configuration ] -------------------------------------------------- #
!/.editorconfig
!/.gitignore
!/.yamllint.yml

# --- [ allowed: top-level documents ] ------------------------------------------------------- #
!/README.md

# --- [ allowed: GitHub configuration ] ------------------------------------------------------ #
!/.github/CODEOWNERS
!/.github/workflows/codeql.yml
!/.github/workflows/powershell.yml

# --- [ allowed: the ansible tree ] ---------------------------------------------------------- #
!/ansible/applications/fileserver/README.md
!/ansible/applications/fileserver/defaults/main.yml
!/ansible/applications/fileserver/files/Set-SmbServerHardening.ps1.stub
!/ansible/applications/fileserver/meta/main.yml
!/ansible/applications/fileserver/tasks/clean_windows.yml
!/ansible/applications/fileserver/tasks/main.yml
!/ansible/applications/fileserver/tasks/present_windows.yml
!/ansible/applications/fileserver/tasks/validate.yml
!/ansible/applications/fileserver/vars/windows.yml
!/ansible/inventory/README.md
!/ansible/playbooks/fileserver-aws.yml

# --- [ allowed: published documentation ] --------------------------------------------------- #
# Enumerated: local working notes live alongside these on disk and are never published.
!/docs/explanation/technical-debt.md
!/docs/reference/ansible-style-guide.md
!/docs/reference/powershell-style-guide.md

# --- [ allowed: scripts ] ------------------------------------------------------------------- #
# The generic script home: PowerShell pairs (one script + one spec — new scripts add both
# lines together) beside Python/bash tooling.
!/scripts/Set-SmbServerHardening.ps1
!/scripts/Set-SmbServerHardening.pester.ps1
!/scripts/materialize-role-scripts.sh

# --- [ never tracked, even by a future allowance ] ------------------------------------------ #
# Composition build tree (framework checkout + overlaid roles) and build worktrees.
/.compose/
/.worktrees/
